    "title": "Two new suspects charged in Towson peeping tom case - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chris Montcalmo ,\n12 hours ago TOWSON, MD—Baltimore County police have charged two additional men in connection with an ongoing investigation into “peeping tom” incidents in the Towson area, officials announced Wednesday.\nDetectives with Precinct 6 issued criminal summonses for Daniel F. Sell, 56, and Johnnie Wade Jr., 53. According to police, both men are suspects in reported incidents that took place in the vicinity of Knollwood Road and the Donnybrook Apartments.\nThe new charges come less than a week after the initial arrest in the case. On May 8, investigators took 55-year-old Andrade Robinson into custody after locating him near a residence in the Rodgers Forge area around 4 a.m.\nIn that instance, detectives were assisted by the Baltimore County Police Department’s Aviation Team to track and apprehend the suspect. Robinson is currently being held without bond at the Baltimore County Detention Center.\nAuthorities have not specified the exact nature of the relationship, if any, between the three men or whether they were acting together. The investigation remains active as detectives continue to look into reports of similar activity throughout the precinct.",
